WEBVTT

00:20.800 --> 00:23.640
[breathing heavily] Clear that shit.
Clear it.

00:23.720 --> 00:25.840
All right. Take her.

00:34.240 --> 00:35.280
[spits and groans]

00:35.360 --> 00:36.200
Shit!

00:39.400 --> 00:42.800
Outside. Till it's done.
Till it's done, brother.

00:42.880 --> 00:44.760
[Linda groaning and panting]

00:46.040 --> 00:47.440
[Tommy] Easy. Easy!

00:47.520 --> 00:48.360
Linda!

00:49.080 --> 00:51.120
I would've taken your bullet.

00:51.640 --> 00:53.120
I deserve the bullet.

00:53.200 --> 00:55.880
An eye for an eye and a tooth for a tooth!

00:55.960 --> 00:57.360
[shushing]

00:58.120 --> 01:00.360
Linda! Linda, look at me.

01:00.440 --> 01:02.280
Linda, you've got a kid.

01:02.360 --> 01:04.840
If you die, he'll come to us to raise.

01:04.920 --> 01:05.800
You hear me?

01:07.880 --> 01:09.120
I used a Derringer.

01:09.200 --> 01:11.160
-All right.
-[shushing]

01:11.240 --> 01:13.360
It's still in there, right above the bone.

01:13.440 --> 01:15.600
[Mosley] Mr Shelby, your guests...

01:15.680 --> 01:17.920
Get him out. Arthur. Family only!

01:18.000 --> 01:18.920
Get him out!

01:20.760 --> 01:22.720
-Mr Shelby, on your behalf--
-Get out!

01:24.440 --> 01:26.480
-Get out!
-[Linda panting]

01:26.560 --> 01:29.480
Lizzie, go to the kitchen,
get some iodine.

01:29.560 --> 01:30.400
Now! Go!

01:30.480 --> 01:31.440
[Linda mumbling]

01:31.520 --> 01:32.400
All right.

01:32.480 --> 01:34.440
[shushing]

01:36.200 --> 01:38.720
-Linda. You'll have to bite on this.
-[Linda groaning]

01:38.800 --> 01:39.760
Linda. Arthur.

01:39.840 --> 01:41.360
Bite! Come here.

01:41.840 --> 01:44.200
[grunts] All right.
Now it's really going to hurt.

01:44.760 --> 01:46.680
-One, two, three.
-[Linda groaning]

01:46.760 --> 01:47.760
[muffled screaming]

01:51.360 --> 01:52.840
-[sobbing and panting]
-[grunts]

01:53.640 --> 01:56.000
[Arthur] All right. All right.

01:56.080 --> 01:58.720
-All right. Almost there.
-[Tommy] Hold her.

01:58.800 --> 02:00.080
[screaming]

02:02.560 --> 02:04.080
[sobbing]

02:06.840 --> 02:08.520
[sobbing] Is she going
to be all right, Tom?

02:09.200 --> 02:10.160
Is she going to be all right, Tom?

02:10.240 --> 02:11.520
-[Tommy] Yeah.
-[Linda panting]

02:11.600 --> 02:12.560
Oh, Jesus.

02:12.640 --> 02:14.600
Arthur, come here. Come here.

02:14.680 --> 02:17.760
If you love her, go to the library,
get some opium.

02:17.840 --> 02:19.640
Go on. She'll be fine. Go, soldier.

02:19.720 --> 02:20.560
[Arthur] Right.

02:21.560 --> 02:22.960
[breathing heavily]

02:25.560 --> 02:28.480
Actually, you can use mine.

02:33.600 --> 02:37.080
Brought a bit to celebrate
the wedding proposal.

02:38.160 --> 02:39.040
Oh!

02:39.120 --> 02:40.280
He proposed, eh?

02:42.960 --> 02:44.000
One knee.

02:45.200 --> 02:46.640
Congratulations, Pol.

02:48.240 --> 02:49.960
Linda. Linda.

02:50.840 --> 02:51.960
You'll have to drink this.

02:52.040 --> 02:54.080
-No, I don't want anything you've touched.
-Twenty-five seconds.

02:54.160 --> 02:57.080
Twenty-five seconds
and the pain will be gone.

02:57.160 --> 02:58.520
Even the pain in your head.

02:59.200 --> 03:00.920
All right, here you go. Drink.

03:07.160 --> 03:08.360
Cushion, Pol.

03:12.480 --> 03:13.400
[Tommy] All right.

03:14.760 --> 03:16.920
-[Linda muttering] Never again.
-[Arthur sobbing]

03:18.040 --> 03:20.360
Jesus Christ!

03:20.920 --> 03:21.760
[Tommy] Arthur.

03:23.200 --> 03:24.440
She's going to be fine.

03:25.640 --> 03:29.160
I gave her something to get her to sleep.
She's going to be fine.

03:32.400 --> 03:33.480
You should have...

03:33.560 --> 03:35.680
You should have let her do it, Pol.

03:36.640 --> 03:38.280
You should have let her do it.

03:40.280 --> 03:41.680
Arthur, come on.

03:42.760 --> 03:44.640
-You should have let her do it.
-Look at me, brother!

03:44.720 --> 03:45.760
Look at me.

03:46.680 --> 03:47.960
You got things to do.

03:48.440 --> 03:49.800
-You've got a kid.
-Yeah.

03:49.880 --> 03:51.760
We need you. All right?

03:51.840 --> 03:53.280
-You understand?
-Yeah.

03:53.760 --> 03:55.680
Aberama wants you as best man.

03:56.520 --> 03:57.520
You hear that?

04:01.160 --> 04:03.480
I save his life, he hugs him.

04:06.240 --> 04:08.000
Oh. [breathing heavily]

04:09.080 --> 04:09.920
I'll do it.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.000
I'll take it.

04:12.560 --> 04:15.000
Right, fine. Let him be. Let him be.

04:20.040 --> 04:21.000
[footsteps receding]

04:23.440 --> 04:24.279
Oh.

04:24.760 --> 04:26.000
[Mosley] Ladies and gentlemen.

04:27.960 --> 04:29.040
Ladies and gentlemen.

04:30.560 --> 04:33.160
I would like to extend our gratitude

04:34.040 --> 04:38.440
to the musicians and the dance company
for your wonderful performance.

04:38.520 --> 04:39.760
[guests murmur]

04:39.840 --> 04:43.280
This has been a wonderful evening.

04:43.360 --> 04:44.200
[man 1] Yes, it has.

04:44.280 --> 04:46.960
And not only for the music
and the dancing.

04:47.480 --> 04:51.800
It has also been about us,
the people gathered here.

04:52.640 --> 04:56.160
English people
in the very heart of England.

04:56.240 --> 04:57.160
[guests express approval]

04:57.760 --> 05:00.120
[Mosley] There are no people
I would rather be among,

05:00.200 --> 05:04.120
no place I would rather be
and no time I would rather be alive.

05:04.200 --> 05:05.040
[man 2] Well said!

05:05.120 --> 05:07.480
Because ever since
the terrible events of October,

05:07.560 --> 05:10.240
when the money markets betrayed us all...

05:10.320 --> 05:11.160
[man 3] Disgrace!

05:11.240 --> 05:15.040
...I have known that change is coming.

05:17.400 --> 05:24.040
The human species has never faced
such immense possibilities, such choices.

05:25.560 --> 05:27.840
In the lives of great nations,

05:29.400 --> 05:31.400
there are moments of destiny

05:33.040 --> 05:36.680
which have swept aside
small men of convention

05:36.760 --> 05:39.720
and discovered men of the moment.

05:39.800 --> 05:40.640
[guests express approval]

05:40.720 --> 05:42.600
-And our host...
-[man 4] Yes.

05:42.680 --> 05:44.120
...is such a man.

05:44.200 --> 05:45.760
[guests express approval and applaud]

05:45.840 --> 05:46.960
[Mosley] For him...

05:48.160 --> 05:52.760
For him, the little calculations
of little men mean nothing.

05:54.120 --> 05:58.520
He is a man well suited to the mighty mood
that England is now in.

05:59.040 --> 06:00.120
[man 5] Hear, hear.

06:01.040 --> 06:06.520
The only reason I say this now,
at this moment on this stage,

06:07.360 --> 06:09.520
is because I have some news.

06:10.000 --> 06:10.840
[guests murmuring]

06:10.920 --> 06:12.880
[chuckles] Good news, I think.

06:12.960 --> 06:14.080
[guests laugh]

06:15.120 --> 06:17.560
[Mosley] I'm sure our host will forgive me
if I use this platform,

06:17.640 --> 06:23.400
this gathering of friends and like minds,
to give you, his trusted allies,

06:23.880 --> 06:26.400
an early announcement
of a long-overdue event.

06:27.440 --> 06:29.920
I want to tell you good folk first

06:31.160 --> 06:33.160
that with the dawn of a new decade,

06:34.840 --> 06:36.880
I will be setting a new course,

06:37.680 --> 06:39.800
setting up a new political movement

06:39.880 --> 06:43.200
-here in the very heart of England.
-[guests express approval]

06:43.280 --> 06:46.600
And Mr Shelby will be with me,
shoulder to shoulder.

06:50.760 --> 06:54.840
It will offer a new conception of politics

06:54.920 --> 06:59.080
in which the great character
of the British, our true character,

06:59.840 --> 07:00.880
will be reborn.

07:08.360 --> 07:11.520
Many of you lost fortunes
in the recent stock market crash.

07:12.560 --> 07:13.800
The men of money,

07:14.600 --> 07:17.000
the capitalists in New York,

07:17.840 --> 07:19.160
the Jews,

07:20.120 --> 07:21.440
the money-power, they...

07:21.520 --> 07:25.080
They run an international system
in which the infinite mobility of money,

07:25.160 --> 07:29.240
its capacity to create
financial chaos and panic,

07:29.800 --> 07:33.800
can bring down any government that dares,
for one moment, to oppose it.

07:35.720 --> 07:40.480
For generations, the efforts
of hardworking men like you

07:40.560 --> 07:43.480
have equipped our competitors against us.

07:43.560 --> 07:46.840
The cotton mills of India,
the cotton mills of Asia,

07:46.920 --> 07:49.360
created with British money

07:49.440 --> 07:53.120
but used for the destruction
of Lancashire and Yorkshire.

07:53.200 --> 07:55.840
-Disgraceful.
-[Mosley] The usurers of New York,

07:55.920 --> 07:59.040
the sweated labour of the Orient,

07:59.120 --> 08:03.000
combining to destroy
the iron and steel factories

08:03.080 --> 08:05.440
of Warwickshire and Staffordshire.

08:05.520 --> 08:09.920
These are policies that could not
be pursued by British statesmen

08:10.000 --> 08:14.240
unless they were mad
or the servants of Jewish finance.

08:14.800 --> 08:16.120
[man 6] Right words. I second that.

08:16.920 --> 08:19.480
They are the ones who took your money,

08:19.560 --> 08:22.680
but it is I and those who know this truth

08:23.160 --> 08:26.560
who will light a flame
the atheists cannot extinguish.

08:26.640 --> 08:28.440
[guests cheering and expressing approval]

08:36.680 --> 08:39.520
The ranks of our heroes of the Great War

08:39.600 --> 08:43.919
have been betrayed again and again
by politicians!

08:44.799 --> 08:49.800
[Mosley] But hear this, those of you
who fought the Jew war for nothing, 

08:49.880 --> 08:51.560
you brave men, 

08:52.120 --> 08:56.960
you will join hands with the angry youth
of Birmingham and Manchester

08:57.040 --> 08:59.120
and London and Liverpool

08:59.200 --> 09:04.600
and declare that England lives tonight
and marches on!

09:04.680 --> 09:05.760
Yes, yes!

09:06.360 --> 09:07.480
[man 7] Well said!

09:07.960 --> 09:09.640
I say all this to you now

09:10.840 --> 09:14.240
because I believe it is
in places like this with people like you

09:14.320 --> 09:16.800
that we will have to pass on
our message directly.

09:17.520 --> 09:20.360
Our message can be summarised
with these words:

09:20.920 --> 09:22.560
"Britain first."

09:22.640 --> 09:23.480
[guests agreeing]

09:24.840 --> 09:26.000
[man 8] As it should be!

09:28.640 --> 09:31.080
And because this is our message,

09:31.160 --> 09:33.560
I doubt it'll be reported fairly
in the press.

09:34.160 --> 09:37.040
I'm afraid the newspapers of this country

09:37.720 --> 09:42.080
are owned by the same vested interests
who took your money.

09:43.640 --> 09:45.960
They sell to the people false news

09:46.040 --> 09:48.200
to raise the interests of the faction

09:48.280 --> 09:51.160
and the section above
the interests of the nation.

09:51.240 --> 09:52.320
Good man.

09:52.840 --> 09:57.760
So hear my words and pass them on
to those with ears to hear,

09:57.840 --> 10:02.400
and be reminded
that when the new decade begins,

10:02.880 --> 10:07.760
there will be the birth of a new
political party which will speak for you!

10:07.840 --> 10:10.400
[man 9] Yes! At last.

10:12.520 --> 10:17.120
This party, this new movement,
this revolution

10:17.840 --> 10:22.320
will be called
the British Union of Fascists.

10:24.520 --> 10:25.520
Well said!

10:25.600 --> 10:27.560
[guests continue applauding and cheering]

10:38.480 --> 10:41.520
What the fuck are you doing
dealing with a man like that, Tommy?

10:42.360 --> 10:45.000
Yeah... You're going to have to trust me.

10:45.560 --> 10:46.680
Again.

10:54.080 --> 10:56.000
I'm going to fuck the Swan.

10:58.120 --> 11:00.440
Somebody go and tell her
to come to my room.

11:01.240 --> 11:02.880
How do you know she'll come?

11:04.800 --> 11:06.400
Because they always do.

11:17.960 --> 11:22.480
Now, forgive me. I'm going to borrow
your husband for a little while.

11:23.760 --> 11:24.800
This way.

11:28.680 --> 11:30.000
[Mosley] Things like tonight,

11:30.560 --> 11:33.480
that shooting, a family dispute in public,

11:34.280 --> 11:36.160
things like that will have to stop.

11:37.000 --> 11:38.520
It's very lower-class.

11:39.120 --> 11:41.240
It's all been cleared up, Mr Mosley.

11:50.360 --> 11:53.280
So, did you learn anything
from my speech tonight?

11:53.960 --> 11:55.080
Yes.

11:55.160 --> 11:56.440
Yes, I learned many things.

11:57.320 --> 12:00.200
[Mosley] Religion was a beast,
but it's dead.

12:00.960 --> 12:03.320
You have to ride the new thing
when it comes.

12:04.040 --> 12:05.320
Like a horse.

12:06.200 --> 12:07.440
You grab it.

12:09.400 --> 12:12.520
I looked into the audience
and I saw medals

12:12.600 --> 12:15.960
and Savile Row suits and bitterness.

12:17.680 --> 12:21.040
They are my people.
Your people will be different.

12:22.600 --> 12:23.440
[scoffs]

12:23.920 --> 12:26.320
Oh, do see the funny side, Shelby.

12:28.920 --> 12:29.960
I do.

12:31.960 --> 12:33.440
I do see the funny side.

12:37.360 --> 12:38.480
[clears throat]

12:39.960 --> 12:41.760
Do you enjoy strategies?

12:42.680 --> 12:43.680
Yes, I do.

12:44.920 --> 12:46.560
Things will begin to happen now.

12:47.200 --> 12:48.040
So...

12:49.480 --> 12:51.760
there are some things we need to discuss.

12:52.720 --> 12:54.720
I have been looking into your companies.

12:55.320 --> 12:57.800
The Shelby portfolio.

12:58.320 --> 13:00.400
Your company lawyer is a Jew.

13:01.360 --> 13:02.760
He will have to go.

13:04.600 --> 13:06.360
-Of course.
-Also,

13:07.480 --> 13:09.360
our friend, Jimmy McCavern,

13:10.000 --> 13:13.240
has asked for control of the racecourses
north of Wincanton.

13:13.720 --> 13:16.920
I decided it is a trifling thing,
considering our new enterprise,

13:17.000 --> 13:19.680
so I said yes.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.200
In return for what?

13:26.000 --> 13:27.200
No return.

13:30.760 --> 13:31.600
None.

13:34.160 --> 13:35.840
When our campaign begins,

13:35.920 --> 13:38.600
the country will be divided
into distinct areas.

13:38.680 --> 13:41.320
McCavern and his men
will be our soldiers in the north,

13:41.800 --> 13:44.200
controlling rallies
and breaking up demonstrations.

13:44.840 --> 13:47.040
In the midlands, it'll be you.

13:47.520 --> 13:49.480
The south, well...

13:49.560 --> 13:50.480
[Tommy clears throat]

13:50.560 --> 13:52.040
I have yet to decide.

13:54.760 --> 13:58.400
Please understand what I'm offering you
as we go forward, Mr Shelby.

13:59.000 --> 14:00.440
When we succeed,

14:01.120 --> 14:03.120
even the king will not be above us.

14:09.360 --> 14:10.880
[sighs] Power.

14:12.560 --> 14:14.720
Like plugging into the mains.

14:15.800 --> 14:17.400
A lighthouse beam.

14:18.520 --> 14:21.440
Your millions of dollars
safe in Switzerland,

14:22.120 --> 14:25.680
and access to every dirty-minded Swan
in England.

14:27.320 --> 14:28.160
Hmm.

14:31.280 --> 14:33.440
Oh, and also, Shelby,

14:34.200 --> 14:35.520
drink less.

15:01.040 --> 15:02.360
[exhales heavily]

15:03.480 --> 15:07.240
♪ I am the key to the lock in your house ♪

15:08.760 --> 15:13.000
♪ That keeps your toys in the basement ♪

15:15.080 --> 15:20.080
♪ And if you get too far inside ♪

15:20.160 --> 15:21.600
[panting]

15:21.680 --> 15:22.640
[whispers] Put it on.

15:25.880 --> 15:27.880
Put the costume back on.

15:31.000 --> 15:36.280
♪ It's always best with the covers up ♪

15:37.120 --> 15:41.520
♪ I am the pick in the ice ♪ 

15:43.520 --> 15:48.960
♪ Do not cry out or hit the alarm ♪

15:50.000 --> 15:54.520
♪ You know we're friends till we die ♪

15:55.840 --> 15:59.080
♪ And either way you turn... ♪

16:00.000 --> 16:03.320
The ballerina and I were wondering
whether perhaps

16:04.600 --> 16:06.480
you might want to join us.

16:06.560 --> 16:09.400
If I told Tommy,
you wouldn't see the morning.

16:09.480 --> 16:11.480
I doubt that very much.

16:12.080 --> 16:16.080
You see, he has been seduced,
just as you were.

16:28.040 --> 16:29.200
[door closes]

16:30.760 --> 16:31.760
[Lizzie] Tommy.

16:34.480 --> 16:35.400
Tommy.

16:36.600 --> 16:37.640
Tom!

16:37.720 --> 16:38.920
What...

16:39.640 --> 16:40.680
Lizzie?

16:41.360 --> 16:42.480
[shouts] What?

16:43.640 --> 16:44.720
[sighs and grunts]

16:44.800 --> 16:46.880
Tommy, I swear to God, you're bad.

16:47.480 --> 16:49.440
That man is fucking evil.

16:49.520 --> 16:50.680
Lizzie...

16:51.920 --> 16:53.360
I'm only doing this

16:54.280 --> 16:55.760
to bring the bastard down.

16:56.240 --> 16:57.240
Yeah, but why?

16:59.360 --> 17:01.280
Tommy, why?

17:02.720 --> 17:04.880
I'm supplying the British government

17:05.600 --> 17:09.079
with information on his organisation,

17:09.160 --> 17:14.520
and in return they are giving me
favourable terms on defence contracts.

17:15.079 --> 17:15.920
No.

17:16.920 --> 17:19.280
You're doing it because you think
somebody should stop him.

17:19.359 --> 17:22.160
-[grunts and clears throat]
-I saw your face when he was speaking.

17:23.560 --> 17:26.119
You're doing it because you think
it's the right thing to do.

17:26.760 --> 17:30.680
All this time, you just did things
that feel nice because you can afford it.

17:30.760 --> 17:33.240
Lizzie, please, please, please, stop.

17:36.400 --> 17:37.800
Don't scare me

17:39.080 --> 17:41.120
by saying you see things in my face.

17:43.440 --> 17:45.880
I still want things that feel nice.

17:50.720 --> 17:51.840
[exhales heavily]

17:53.520 --> 17:54.960
[Linda gasps and coughs]

17:55.760 --> 17:56.840
[groaning]

17:57.600 --> 17:58.760
[Arthur sighs]

18:06.760 --> 18:08.040
-Linda.
-Arthur.

18:09.640 --> 18:11.280
[Arthur shushing]

18:15.480 --> 18:16.560
Linda.

18:18.320 --> 18:19.320
Let's go.

18:21.600 --> 18:23.200
Let's go. Let's leave.

18:24.320 --> 18:25.440
Let's get in the car.

18:26.080 --> 18:27.680
We'll go and pick up Billy.

18:29.040 --> 18:30.800
We'll drive to the docks.

18:31.640 --> 18:33.000
Any dock you want.

18:35.440 --> 18:36.640
We'll get on a boat.

18:37.240 --> 18:38.560
We'll sail away.

18:39.120 --> 18:40.200
You and me.

18:41.400 --> 18:43.080
Any destination.

18:43.720 --> 18:44.880
[groaning]

18:50.360 --> 18:51.800
Be careful, it's...

18:52.720 --> 18:54.480
It's broken everywhere.

18:57.040 --> 18:59.320
We leave tonight. Hmm?

19:00.760 --> 19:02.160
We leave this place.

19:03.160 --> 19:05.000
We never come back, Linda.

19:05.800 --> 19:07.200
We never come back.

19:09.080 --> 19:10.360
I mean that.

19:13.760 --> 19:15.840
We go before it gets light.

19:18.200 --> 19:19.600
Say yes.

19:21.280 --> 19:23.480
-I've got a better idea.
-Yeah?

19:26.840 --> 19:28.240
You stay here...

19:29.920 --> 19:32.600
living inside your head,

19:33.480 --> 19:35.840
inside your knife, inside your war.

19:39.120 --> 19:40.040
[Arthur breathes deeply]

19:44.200 --> 19:46.200
I'm glad I didn't shoot you.

19:51.000 --> 19:52.720
It would've been a kindness.

20:02.480 --> 20:03.880
[sobbing] Now, get out.

20:06.280 --> 20:07.840
-Oh, please.
-[inhales sharply]

20:09.600 --> 20:10.840
[glass crunching]

20:14.760 --> 20:15.600
[sniffling]

20:22.520 --> 20:23.880
-[door opens]
-[breathes shakily]

20:24.960 --> 20:26.200
[door closes]

20:48.640 --> 20:49.720
[groans]

21:11.000 --> 21:12.000
[car engine running]

21:13.320 --> 21:14.360
[car door opens]

21:20.600 --> 21:23.600
An evening with
a bunch of fucking Gypsies.

21:26.760 --> 21:27.600
[sighs]

21:46.200 --> 21:47.240
[children chattering]

21:47.720 --> 21:49.000
[boy] I will shoot!

21:50.160 --> 21:51.840
Peter! Peter! Kick it here!

21:58.120 --> 21:59.320
[boy] Kick it here, mister!

22:08.680 --> 22:10.040
[Tommy] This is a cheque guarantee. 

22:10.680 --> 22:11.920
Signed by Mosley

22:13.200 --> 22:16.560
on behalf of a man called Jimmy McCavern.

22:16.640 --> 22:17.640
A cheque for what?

22:17.720 --> 22:20.960
Well, I said it was
for the sale of a gin distillery.

22:21.640 --> 22:22.800
But it doesn't matter.

22:24.280 --> 22:27.120
It is direct evidence
of a link between Mosley

22:27.200 --> 22:29.560
and the head
of an organised criminal network.

22:30.400 --> 22:33.560
A relationship he will try to deny

22:34.240 --> 22:36.840
after the bonfire of all conventions.

22:37.880 --> 22:40.880
It also contains the names of MPs
who have signed up to the movement.

22:41.440 --> 22:43.960
And those MPs who are sympathetic

22:44.040 --> 22:48.640
but will not show their hand until
the organisation is announced officially.

22:49.520 --> 22:51.200
On the second of January.

22:52.320 --> 22:53.480
In Grosvenor House.

22:53.560 --> 22:55.080
You might want to write some of this down.

22:55.160 --> 22:58.480
I am experiencing resistance
from my superior officers, too.

23:03.000 --> 23:05.120
This isn't intelligence, Younger.

23:06.200 --> 23:07.560
This is evidence.

23:08.360 --> 23:09.320
Give it to the Branch.

23:09.400 --> 23:10.800
Special Branch?

23:10.880 --> 23:13.720
Half of whom spend their lives defending
the Union against Fenians,

23:13.800 --> 23:15.000
and the other half who spend their lives

23:15.080 --> 23:17.360
defending men like Mosley
against socialists.

23:17.880 --> 23:20.560
I heard about his speech
at your house the other night.

23:20.640 --> 23:24.840
It was favourably reported as
the passionate and spontaneous outpouring

23:24.920 --> 23:27.640
of a man moved by
the emotions of a ballet.

23:28.200 --> 23:31.520
-Reported where?
-Daily Mail, Morning Post, Daily Mirror.

23:32.040 --> 23:36.320
It's upper, middle, and working class,
all united in admiration.

23:39.200 --> 23:43.240
Also, I'm being asked the source
of my information on Mosley.

23:43.760 --> 23:45.920
-Which you don't divulge.
-No.

23:47.120 --> 23:50.320
As a result, my six-monthly review
was unfavourable.

23:51.800 --> 23:55.480
They're talking about moving me to
a black and coloured desk in Johannesburg.

23:56.960 --> 24:00.080
I also suspect there are specific threats
to me personally

24:01.160 --> 24:03.400
from an organisation called "Section D".

24:04.600 --> 24:06.880
I believe you've had a dispute
with them in the past.

24:09.040 --> 24:10.240
Sit down, Younger.

24:16.240 --> 24:17.280
[sighs]

24:19.440 --> 24:20.280
[mutters]

24:25.600 --> 24:27.280
We are now Section D.

24:28.240 --> 24:29.560
I fucking beat them.

24:32.560 --> 24:34.560
You're a soldier, I'm a soldier.

24:35.160 --> 24:39.920
There are elements within the state
who are prepared to kill.

24:40.600 --> 24:42.600
We need to meet them unafraid.

24:43.120 --> 24:43.960
[scoffs]

24:46.720 --> 24:48.200
Spoken like a true believer.

24:50.440 --> 24:54.360
My superiors also ask why the information
on Jessie Eden and the communists

24:54.440 --> 24:56.200
has apparently dried up.

24:57.440 --> 24:59.440
Why has it dried up, Mr Shelby?

25:01.000 --> 25:02.960
Your sister has an interesting theory.

25:03.480 --> 25:06.520
She thinks perhaps at last Tommy Shelby

25:06.600 --> 25:08.880
has actually started
to believe in something.

25:20.760 --> 25:21.680
Younger.

25:23.600 --> 25:26.320
Please don't listen
to my sister's opinions of me.

25:26.880 --> 25:28.280
They are always...

25:29.200 --> 25:30.200
hopeful.

25:31.760 --> 25:33.840
Therefore, they are always wrong.

25:34.880 --> 25:35.720
[scoffs]

25:42.560 --> 25:43.400
[door opens]

25:44.440 --> 25:45.280
[door closes]

25:46.720 --> 25:47.680
[children laughing]

25:53.440 --> 25:54.680
[breathing deeply]

26:08.400 --> 26:09.520
[children shouting]

26:18.720 --> 26:19.760
[gasps]

26:28.080 --> 26:28.920
[exhales heavily]

26:48.000 --> 26:49.200
[exhales sharply]

27:13.120 --> 27:14.840
Can you hear me? Look at me.

27:14.920 --> 27:16.720
You're going to be all right.
I'll be back.

27:16.800 --> 27:17.760
You'll be okay.

27:18.280 --> 27:20.880
Look at me. It's okay. It's all right.

27:26.360 --> 27:27.200
Fuck.

27:28.040 --> 27:32.000
Call an ambulance! Call Moss!
Find out where I can reach him.

27:32.080 --> 27:34.000
Come on, love. Up you get.

27:34.080 --> 27:36.080
Good girl. Come on.
Take her. Take her.

27:37.480 --> 27:41.360
Come on. Up you get.
Up you get. Good boy.

27:41.880 --> 27:43.560
Come on. In you go.

27:43.640 --> 27:45.400
Inside. Stay inside.

27:54.120 --> 27:55.160
[panting]

28:29.720 --> 28:30.560
[door opens]

28:33.400 --> 28:34.240
[door closes]

28:38.520 --> 28:39.600
Tommy?

28:40.160 --> 28:41.720
Let's sit down, Ada.

28:41.800 --> 28:43.000
What's happened?

28:44.840 --> 28:45.680
Here.

28:46.200 --> 28:47.120
Sit down, eh?

28:57.520 --> 28:59.040
Ben Younger is dead.

29:02.280 --> 29:04.120
Someone put a bomb in his car.

29:07.840 --> 29:12.400
I don't know how you felt about him
or how bad this is going to hurt,

29:13.880 --> 29:16.880
but whatever happens, just remember
you have a baby inside of you.

29:21.800 --> 29:22.840
God.

29:24.760 --> 29:26.560
Anyone you touch.

29:28.120 --> 29:29.960
Which means anyone I touch.

29:31.440 --> 29:33.680
Which means anyone any of us touch.

29:34.960 --> 29:37.200
He never knew I was pregnant.

29:37.920 --> 29:39.040
I hadn't told him.

29:40.360 --> 29:42.880
[sighs heavily] God, I didn't love him.

29:45.160 --> 29:46.720
But I liked him.

29:48.920 --> 29:51.680
He was decent and good.

29:54.800 --> 29:57.040
And I wasn't going to marry him.

30:00.000 --> 30:02.560
The baby was a mistake, but that's okay...

30:04.800 --> 30:06.120
because I didn't

30:06.800 --> 30:08.720
ask anything of him.

30:10.280 --> 30:12.360
God, he didn't deserve us.

30:16.680 --> 30:18.440
Well, I've spoken to his family.

30:18.520 --> 30:20.320
They're going to take care of the funeral.

30:21.040 --> 30:21.880
[sniffles]

30:21.960 --> 30:26.560
It will go down as an IRA assassination
of a British military officer.

30:29.400 --> 30:30.880
And what was it really?

30:34.240 --> 30:36.320
[smacks lips and breathes deeply]

30:36.400 --> 30:37.800
It was...

30:39.120 --> 30:41.240
a consequence of good intentions.

30:42.120 --> 30:43.760
My good intentions.

30:45.080 --> 30:45.960
[scoffs]

30:46.040 --> 30:49.400
I pushed him to report on the fascists.
I thought it was the right thing to do.

30:51.200 --> 30:56.920
And as a result, Section D or the Branch
or Intelligence had him killed.

30:58.400 --> 30:59.240
[scoffs]

31:10.560 --> 31:11.960
There was a kid,

31:12.840 --> 31:14.480
died in the explosion.

31:15.360 --> 31:16.880
He was ten years old.

31:18.760 --> 31:20.040
It's funny...

31:21.480 --> 31:23.440
isn't it? How it works?

31:23.960 --> 31:26.440
[breathes deeply and clears throat]

31:26.520 --> 31:27.760
[Ada] No, Tommy.

31:30.240 --> 31:32.800
Don't give yourself this excuse.

31:37.320 --> 31:39.120
He was ten years old.

31:40.520 --> 31:42.320
If I would have stuck to what I do,

31:43.320 --> 31:45.480
he'd still be kicking
a ball in the street.

31:47.000 --> 31:48.320
[thunder rumbling]

31:48.400 --> 31:49.720
It's funny, isn't it?

31:53.440 --> 31:54.400
[breathing heavily]

32:00.880 --> 32:01.720
[sniffles]

32:12.240 --> 32:13.240
[tense music playing]

32:13.320 --> 32:14.200
[exhales sharply]

32:34.280 --> 32:35.120
[sniffles]

32:47.360 --> 32:48.800
Push the button,

32:49.840 --> 32:52.320
unlock the door, and come home to me.

32:58.040 --> 32:58.880
[engine starts]

33:14.120 --> 33:15.240
[boat engine chugging]

33:16.200 --> 33:18.880
Chinese lanterns! Brass on deck!

33:21.080 --> 33:22.600
God fucking help us.

33:35.160 --> 33:36.000
[grunts]

33:54.680 --> 33:57.120
[Aberama] Chang will be waiting
at the dock with the cargo.

33:57.720 --> 33:59.760
We weigh it, we load it, we fuck off.

34:00.720 --> 34:01.560
[scoffs]

34:15.880 --> 34:17.679
[Arthur] Where the fuck is Chang?

34:25.880 --> 34:27.440
Isiah, take point.

34:28.360 --> 34:29.560
Look lively.

34:32.400 --> 34:34.760
Right. There's your lanterns.

34:35.360 --> 34:37.440
Where the fuck are the Chinese?

34:37.520 --> 34:38.520
All right.

34:38.600 --> 34:39.880
[man coughing]

34:39.960 --> 34:41.400
Arthur, it's Chang.

34:41.480 --> 34:42.600
[indistinct shouting]

34:43.360 --> 34:44.440
[indistinct shouting]

34:46.960 --> 34:48.440
Get over. Get over! Get over!

34:50.239 --> 34:53.040
I knew we shouldn't trust these fuckers
and their fucking lanterns.

34:54.960 --> 34:56.000
[groans]

35:00.239 --> 35:04.360
If it's police, hold fire.
Chang, where's the stuff? Where is it?

35:04.920 --> 35:06.240
They didn't look like police.

35:06.320 --> 35:07.400
Smelled of gin.

35:07.480 --> 35:10.560
They said they were taking the opium
on behalf of the king.

35:10.640 --> 35:12.480
Then they saw your boat coming.

35:12.560 --> 35:14.040
So, were they Italian?

35:14.960 --> 35:16.640
-Were they Italian?
-Irish.

35:17.520 --> 35:19.600
-Irish, I think.
-Oh, fuck.

35:19.680 --> 35:20.680
Fuck!

35:21.880 --> 35:24.560
Curly, my gun. Give me the gun.
Give it up! That's it.

35:24.640 --> 35:26.640
Listen. Listen to me!

35:26.720 --> 35:29.200
They're Titanic boys out there, all right?

35:29.280 --> 35:32.960
They're out of Poplar.
In the war, they were very capable.

35:33.040 --> 35:34.880
Very capable soldiers.

35:35.480 --> 35:36.480
So was I.

35:37.080 --> 35:39.280
I was a fucking capable soldier, too.

35:40.120 --> 35:41.480
Hey!

35:41.560 --> 35:44.000
Hey, you fucking bastards!

36:03.480 --> 36:07.320
Arthur! Arthur! Stop firing!
Arthur, they're gone.

36:07.400 --> 36:08.920
[breathing heavily and grunting]

36:12.520 --> 36:14.480
To any of you still alive,

36:15.200 --> 36:21.360
you do not fuck
with the Peaky fucking Blinders.

36:22.040 --> 36:23.720
[chuckles] Oh.

36:23.800 --> 36:24.640
[door opens]

36:29.040 --> 36:30.800
[Chang coughs and breathes heavily]

36:36.080 --> 36:36.920
[grunts]

36:45.000 --> 36:45.840
[Arthur scoffs]

36:47.840 --> 36:48.800
Yeah.

36:51.640 --> 36:52.480
[sighs]

36:52.560 --> 36:53.480
[Charlie] Here we go.

36:56.960 --> 36:57.800
[grunts]

36:59.120 --> 37:00.640
[sniffles] Hmm.

37:02.360 --> 37:03.200
Chang.

37:08.000 --> 37:09.400
Purest ever in Europe.

37:09.480 --> 37:12.680
Arthur, there's a dead man
in a copper's uniform.

37:13.240 --> 37:14.560
Should I throw him in the cut?

37:16.000 --> 37:16.840
No.

37:17.440 --> 37:18.800
No, he'll float, won't he?

37:19.720 --> 37:21.760
Even Irishmen fucking float.

37:23.000 --> 37:24.440
No. Go and find a...

37:24.960 --> 37:26.360
Go and find a kiln or something.

37:26.840 --> 37:28.480
But there are men working them.

37:30.000 --> 37:33.120
Why do you carry a gun, Isiah, eh?

37:33.800 --> 37:35.520
Or razor blades in your cap?

37:37.320 --> 37:39.840
Because you're a Peaky fucking Blinder,
that's why.

37:40.840 --> 37:43.560
You take that body
and you burn it to the bone.

37:44.120 --> 37:46.560
And if anybody speaks to you on that,

37:47.640 --> 37:51.000
you offer them the chance
to burn in that furnace with him.

37:52.000 --> 37:52.840
All right?

37:53.480 --> 37:54.320
Yes, Arthur.

37:56.320 --> 37:57.280
[Arthur] Yeah.

37:58.000 --> 37:58.840
Yeah.

37:59.400 --> 38:01.560
Do we know the people
who tried to trick us?

38:02.200 --> 38:03.320
The uncles will be mad.

38:03.400 --> 38:07.320
Fuck your uncles. And your aunts,
your cousins, all of them. Right?

38:08.920 --> 38:11.720
Curly, load this up onto the boat.

38:12.240 --> 38:13.720
Let's get back to Birmingham, eh?

38:14.280 --> 38:16.440
Get back to fucking civilisation.

38:16.520 --> 38:19.360
And find out who's been talking. Yeah.

38:19.440 --> 38:22.480
Now, look. The Titanic heard
about this, right?

38:23.120 --> 38:27.240
That means every gang from Poplar
to Birmingham will be here.

38:28.920 --> 38:30.200
Well, let them come.

38:31.000 --> 38:33.080
Let them come, Aberama! [inhales sharply]

38:33.160 --> 38:34.520
Yeah.

38:34.600 --> 38:36.760
Oh, let them fucking come.

38:40.480 --> 38:41.320
Yeah.

38:42.120 --> 38:48.880
♪ Walk in silence ♪

38:49.520 --> 38:52.960
♪ Don't walk away ♪

38:53.720 --> 38:56.800
♪ In silence ♪

38:57.600 --> 39:00.720
♪ See the danger ♪

39:01.880 --> 39:05.120
♪ Always danger ♪

39:05.840 --> 39:08.720
♪ Endless talking ♪

39:09.720 --> 39:12.520
♪ Life rebuilding ♪

39:13.600 --> 39:15.760
♪ Don't walk away ♪

39:23.240 --> 39:28.280
♪ People like you find it easy ♪

39:29.160 --> 39:31.960
♪ Naked to see ♪

39:33.360 --> 39:35.720
♪ Walking on air ♪

39:37.560 --> 39:39.760
♪ Don't walk away ♪

39:41.840 --> 39:44.920
♪ In silence ♪

39:45.520 --> 39:48.000
♪ Don't walk away ♪

39:57.800 --> 39:59.360
[indistinct shouting in distance]

40:10.960 --> 40:12.480
Hat and coat off.

40:24.720 --> 40:26.600
Stand up against the wall.

40:30.800 --> 40:34.480
For your own safety,
I need to search you for items

40:34.560 --> 40:37.400
that could potentially be used
as weapons against you.

40:54.920 --> 40:56.240
Oh, that's nice.

41:16.080 --> 41:17.560
He was my friend.

41:18.080 --> 41:20.400
Yeah, well he's nobody's friend anymore.

41:20.480 --> 41:22.000
He's a fucking animal.

41:22.960 --> 41:25.440
Laces out of your shoes.

41:26.280 --> 41:27.560
[indistinct screaming in distance]

41:38.840 --> 41:39.800
Table.

41:53.120 --> 41:54.880
[man 1 screaming]

42:01.200 --> 42:02.920
[man 2 screaming]

42:07.760 --> 42:10.160
Barney! Visitor.

42:10.960 --> 42:13.320
This one's real. [chuckles]

42:13.880 --> 42:14.960
You can wait here.

42:15.440 --> 42:17.520
No. I can't.

42:25.560 --> 42:28.320
It's your funeral.
I'll have to lock you in.

42:28.400 --> 42:29.240
Yeah.

42:36.880 --> 42:37.720
[door locks]

42:52.960 --> 42:54.080
Hello, Barney.

42:55.520 --> 42:56.960
Arthur says to say "hello".

42:59.080 --> 43:00.160
Sergeant Major?

43:02.160 --> 43:03.240
You're alive?

43:04.040 --> 43:07.480
Arthur's alive, John's dead,
Danny's dead, Freddie's dead,

43:08.720 --> 43:11.320
Jeremiah preaches the gospel barefoot.

43:12.720 --> 43:13.560
Yeah.

43:14.840 --> 43:15.960
And I'm alive.

43:20.080 --> 43:21.960
Thems who're gone are the lucky ones.

43:26.280 --> 43:28.680
Thanks for the letters
you send, Sergeant Major.

43:28.760 --> 43:30.640
Yeah, Arthur mostly writes them. I just...

43:31.240 --> 43:32.160
just sign them.

43:34.280 --> 43:36.960
How the fuck do you write back?
With your fucking teeth?

43:37.040 --> 43:38.800
No, they stick a pen up me arse.

43:38.880 --> 43:39.720
[chuckles]

43:51.600 --> 43:52.960
[sighs heavily]

43:53.040 --> 43:54.880
Someone in here said your name.

43:56.480 --> 43:59.280
They said out there
you are a politician now.

43:59.360 --> 44:00.720
Sometimes, yeah.

44:03.120 --> 44:05.160
Didn't know if it was real, comrade.

44:06.840 --> 44:09.880
I see rats coming out of bodies
like at the black wood.

44:10.440 --> 44:12.080
The shit they give me in here...

44:19.480 --> 44:21.320
Hey, Barney. Look at me.

44:30.440 --> 44:32.680
Barney, this here is opium and cyanide.

44:33.400 --> 44:34.480
Bring on a heart attack.

44:35.520 --> 44:37.960
They won't even check the cause.
You won't feel a fucking thing.

44:44.440 --> 44:45.320
So, here.

44:48.560 --> 44:50.040
You're in here forever, brother.

44:51.640 --> 44:53.600
Don't have the use of your fucking hands.

44:55.640 --> 44:57.080
You're still in the tunnels.

44:58.480 --> 45:00.520
I can give this to you now.

45:03.200 --> 45:04.200
You want it?

45:05.080 --> 45:05.960
[breathing shakily]

45:09.840 --> 45:10.680
No.

45:26.640 --> 45:27.640
Why not?

45:33.360 --> 45:34.400
I know.

45:37.320 --> 45:38.320
I know.

45:40.880 --> 45:44.560
You still remember that French waitress.

45:44.640 --> 45:45.480
[sobbing]

45:53.840 --> 45:55.560
You still going on about that, Tom?

45:56.080 --> 45:56.960
Yeah.

45:57.960 --> 45:58.920
Did you fuck her before me?

45:59.000 --> 46:00.560
Because whoever did
gave me the fucking clap,

46:00.640 --> 46:01.800
and I'm guessing it was you.

46:02.360 --> 46:04.400
-Yes, I fucked her before you did.
-Yeah.

46:07.320 --> 46:08.560
She was beautiful.

46:08.640 --> 46:10.320
She was. She was.

46:12.400 --> 46:15.200
And I reckon I was second best
after Barney.

46:16.640 --> 46:18.040
Why did you bring the capsule, Tom?

46:18.120 --> 46:19.680
You're in here, Barney.

46:20.600 --> 46:22.040
You have no hands.

46:22.520 --> 46:23.920
There is no daylight.

46:25.040 --> 46:26.440
And you don't want to die.

46:27.800 --> 46:29.040
No, I don't.

46:33.680 --> 46:35.720
Because one day things might change.

46:46.280 --> 46:47.280
Yeah.

46:49.320 --> 46:50.720
Things might change.

46:54.200 --> 46:55.760
Maybe they already have.

46:57.800 --> 46:58.720
Come here, Barney.

47:00.680 --> 47:01.520
Come here.

47:05.320 --> 47:07.000
What if I could break you out of here?

47:08.280 --> 47:09.960
Why would you break me out?

47:11.360 --> 47:14.720
See, the trouble with the people in here
is the fucking meds they keep you on.

47:17.040 --> 47:19.720
Ten years since we're back.

47:19.800 --> 47:21.880
Barney, ten fucking years.

47:23.680 --> 47:25.160
Maybe the storm has passed.

47:25.240 --> 47:26.720
Passed for you then, has it, Tom?

47:29.400 --> 47:31.120
What would the world do with me
if I was out?

47:31.200 --> 47:32.320
I have a job for you.

47:33.120 --> 47:33.960
[laughs]

47:34.680 --> 47:36.160
-Fuck.
-Barney.

47:38.080 --> 47:41.840
Barney, you were the best fucking sniper
in our company. Never missed.

47:43.000 --> 47:44.400
I can use that man.

47:45.880 --> 47:50.240
Get you the latest BSA,
fucking telescopic sights.

47:51.520 --> 47:52.360
Who am I shooting?

47:52.440 --> 47:55.760
The fuck do you care, Barney?
Get that fucking thing off.

47:55.840 --> 47:56.680
Get you free.

47:56.760 --> 47:58.200
-[banging on door]
-[nurse] You all right in there?

47:58.280 --> 47:59.400
Grand in here.

48:03.480 --> 48:04.640
What do you say, Barney?

48:06.640 --> 48:07.800
I'll come for you

48:08.520 --> 48:10.000
after midnight on Wednesday.

48:10.760 --> 48:12.320
I don't keep track of days, Tom.

48:12.400 --> 48:13.400
Don't have to.

48:13.480 --> 48:16.720
You'll know it will be Wednesday
because there'll be a big fucking bang.

48:17.360 --> 48:19.040
All right. [chuckles excitedly]

48:21.760 --> 48:22.600
[banging on door]

48:23.720 --> 48:25.240
Big fucking bang.

48:26.000 --> 48:27.360
Big fucking bang.

48:27.440 --> 48:29.760
Big fucking bang. [chuckles]

48:33.560 --> 48:38.080
♪ Generals gathered in their masses ♪

48:38.760 --> 48:43.720
♪ Just like witches at black masses ♪

48:44.320 --> 48:49.440
♪ Evil minds that plot destruction ♪

48:49.520 --> 48:54.600
♪ Sorcerers of death's construction ♪

48:55.320 --> 49:00.080
♪ No more war pigs have the power ♪

49:00.680 --> 49:05.040
♪ Hand of God has struck the hour ♪

49:05.600 --> 49:09.920
♪ Time will tell on their power minds ♪

49:10.000 --> 49:11.760
-[explosion]
-[men shouting]

49:14.480 --> 49:16.280
It's fucking Wednesday!

49:18.960 --> 49:21.120
[laughing] Big bang on Wednesday!

49:34.960 --> 49:36.120
[footsteps approaching]

49:40.440 --> 49:42.440
They called from the Black Boy in Knowle.

49:43.200 --> 49:44.600
They'll be here any minute.

49:45.840 --> 49:47.920
I hear you agreed to give up the north.

49:49.480 --> 49:52.720
I hear there needs to be some certainty
in the south.

49:53.640 --> 49:56.920
Some of my people were attacked
by members of the Titanic.

49:57.000 --> 49:58.400
They've heard about the cargo.

49:59.320 --> 50:03.080
Mr Mosley is open to suggestion
regarding who he can rely on

50:03.160 --> 50:04.840
to offer him support in London.

50:05.520 --> 50:10.040
Well, I would suggest the most competent
organiser of men in the south

50:10.120 --> 50:11.480
is Alfie Solomons.

50:11.560 --> 50:12.520
[scoffs]

50:13.120 --> 50:14.240
He's dead.

50:16.040 --> 50:17.360
And he's Jewish.

50:18.480 --> 50:21.120
And I'd say as far as our boss
is concerned,

50:21.200 --> 50:24.600
him being dead would be less
of an obstacle than him being Jewish.

50:26.120 --> 50:28.360
I think he'll give London to the Italians.

50:29.280 --> 50:30.760
He likes Italians.

50:32.080 --> 50:34.160
That'll mean more concessions
on your part,

50:34.240 --> 50:37.160
but you're going to have to accept it,
tinker boy.

50:37.240 --> 50:38.080
[sniffs]

50:39.520 --> 50:40.920
I like Wincanton.

50:41.640 --> 50:43.360
It's a grand old racecourse.

50:45.880 --> 50:46.880
That brother of yours,

50:47.960 --> 50:49.880
the one who lent me a hand grenade...

50:52.240 --> 50:54.440
he'd be the first
of you tinkers I'd go for

50:54.520 --> 50:56.840
if our truce should end
and the whistle blew.

50:57.640 --> 50:58.480
Good.

50:59.240 --> 51:00.920
He's in the mood for a quarrel.

51:03.960 --> 51:06.280
We had a brush with the Titanic, Tom.

51:06.360 --> 51:07.200
Yeah, I heard.

51:07.280 --> 51:08.400
Yeah.

51:08.480 --> 51:09.600
Fun night.

51:10.160 --> 51:11.160
Got noisy, though.

51:11.240 --> 51:12.080
[grunts]

51:12.680 --> 51:15.880
And to think they all said I was mad
to take me dad with me, eh?

51:16.520 --> 51:18.040
Your dad? Who's your dad?

51:18.520 --> 51:20.000
This is my fucking dad.

51:21.120 --> 51:22.240
Right here.

51:22.960 --> 51:24.680
This is my fucking dad.

51:24.760 --> 51:25.960
Where's Aberama?

51:28.080 --> 51:29.400
He got off at Solihull.

51:31.000 --> 51:33.320
Said if he sees Billy Boy here,
[inhales sharply]

51:34.640 --> 51:36.320
he'll cut his fucking throat.

51:37.120 --> 51:39.840
Tell the tinker he's welcome
to come and try at any time.

51:39.920 --> 51:40.760
Hmm.

51:41.520 --> 51:42.440
Is it all aboard?

51:43.040 --> 51:43.920
[breathing heavily]

51:47.400 --> 51:48.400
Yeah.

51:49.320 --> 51:50.240
It's all there.

51:51.000 --> 51:52.720
We weighed it at the wharf.

51:52.800 --> 51:53.960
We used Cockney scales.

51:54.040 --> 51:56.040
I wouldn't trust them,
they're probably crooked.

51:57.240 --> 51:58.520
But, er...

51:58.600 --> 52:00.440
I reckon seven tons.

52:00.520 --> 52:01.560
Curly!

52:03.160 --> 52:06.280
Put ten sacks of flour
onto Mr McCavern's boat.

52:06.800 --> 52:07.800
Tom...

52:08.320 --> 52:09.960
I don't think it's really flour.

52:10.040 --> 52:11.880
I know, Curly. Just do as I say.

52:12.440 --> 52:13.280
Yeah. Yeah.

52:13.800 --> 52:14.800
Curly.

52:20.000 --> 52:21.040
[McCavern] Hey, Arthur.

52:21.880 --> 52:23.440
Someday, yes?

52:23.920 --> 52:24.920
You and me?

52:26.760 --> 52:28.160
Oh, Tommy, eh?

52:28.960 --> 52:31.200
Fascists. Hmm? [chuckles]

52:32.240 --> 52:33.400
Look at them.

52:34.200 --> 52:35.520
I fucking hate them,

52:36.040 --> 52:37.280
always have done.

52:38.760 --> 52:40.520
But you? [chuckles]

52:41.080 --> 52:42.560
You, Billy Boy.

52:43.200 --> 52:46.240
Oh, you're special.
You know, I fucking like him, Tommy.

52:46.720 --> 52:47.720
I like you.

52:48.600 --> 52:50.960
I do. You're a man after me own heart.

52:51.040 --> 52:52.800
-Someday, Mr Shelby.
-Yeah.

52:52.880 --> 52:53.720
-Someday.
-Yeah.

52:55.080 --> 52:55.920
Yeah.

53:02.440 --> 53:03.880
You just tell me when, Tom.

53:05.000 --> 53:06.360
You just tell me when.

53:09.520 --> 53:10.360
So...

53:11.200 --> 53:14.120
-So, you spoke to Barney Thomason, eh?
-Yeah.

53:16.320 --> 53:17.720
Barney Thomason...

53:19.040 --> 53:23.000
is going to kill Oswald Mosley. [scoffs]

53:23.080 --> 53:24.560
Shoot him in the fucking head.

53:25.280 --> 53:26.120
Yep.

53:27.520 --> 53:30.880
While he's onstage.
While I'm stood next to him.

53:32.640 --> 53:35.240
And then I will take over
as the leader of the party,

53:36.480 --> 53:39.680
and you and Aberama
can take care of that bastard, McCavern.

53:41.560 --> 53:45.280
I had more complicated strategies
in mind for Mr Mosley.

53:46.480 --> 53:48.400
Then he spoke badly to my wife.

53:50.400 --> 53:52.600
It's going to be
a busy few weeks, brother.

53:52.680 --> 53:53.520
Yeah.

54:07.720 --> 54:09.720
[theme music playing]

54:24.040 --> 54:28.360
♪ On a gathering storm
Comes a tall handsome man ♪

54:28.440 --> 54:32.600
♪ In a dusty black coat
With a red right hand ♪

54:40.320 --> 54:45.040
♪ A shadow is cast wherever he stands ♪
